    Option C—the sync script paired with KDE's native slideshow—is the most straightforward and reliable path since it avoids custom plugin complexity. But Option A, a proper QML-based Plasma plugin that talks directly to the Jellyfin API, would feel more polished and work seamlessly across both the desktop and lock screen. I should give a clear recommendation based on what matters most here.
